cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Supplementary material for "A machine-learning surrogate for rapid
  hazard-zone prediction of n-hexane vapor dispersion from tank overfill"
message: >-
  If you use this data or these parameters in work you publish, please cite the
  journal article in the preferred-citation field below.
type: dataset
license: MIT
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/Melionidas31/jlp-hexane-surrogate-supplementary
abstract: >-
  Complete parameters of two artificial neural network surrogates of the ALOHA
  dispersion code, predicting the red, orange and yellow hazard-zone radii of
  an n-hexane vapour cloud released by tank overfill. Includes the 1,215 and
  1,261 scenario ALOHA simulation datasets the surrogates were fitted on and a
  script that checks the parameters against the data.
keywords:
  - process safety
  - surrogate model
  - ALOHA
  - dispersion modelling
  - neural network
  - n-hexane
  - hazard zone
  - reproducibility
